abstract: >-
  Maple worksheets, MATLAB and Julia solvers, Mathematica notebooks, Python programs and data for the quasinormal modes
  of massless scalar, electromagnetic and gravitational perturbations of Schwarzschild–de Sitter black holes, for
  dimensionless cosmological constants between 0.02 and 0.11, and of their Nariai limit. After the behaviour at the
  event and cosmological horizons is factored out, a Chebyshev collocation turns the radial problem into a quadratic
  eigenvalue problem, and only the roots on which three resolutions agree are kept; in the Nariai limit a root is kept
  when the Jost Wronskian of the Pöschl–Teller problem vanishes there. Independent Python programs follow oscillatory
  and purely imaginary branches towards the Nariai limit by collocation and by Frobenius matching at the two horizons,
  test convergence up to 300 Chebyshev modes in double and 70-digit arithmetic, compare the axial and polar spectra,
  compute the Schwarzschild modes by Leaver's continued fraction and verify the algebra exactly.
